An unused result-generic template whose result a concrete provider already
produces names that shadowing producer, instead of the misleading "no consumer
pins its result type": a consumer does pin Box[int], it is just satisfied by
ConcreteBox first, leaving MakeBox genuinely unused. Erroring is correct; the
message points at the real cause.
-- config --
import-path: example.com/app
package-name: app
error-is: ErrUnusedTemplate
-- example.com/app/a.go --
package app

type Box[T any] struct{}

//plumb:build
func ConcreteBox() Box[int] { return Box[int]{} }

//plumb:build
func MakeBox[T any]() Box[T] { return Box[T]{} }

//plumb:build
func Use(b Box[int]) int { return 0 }
